## 6. Modular ownership boundaries

Preserve this split:

```text
runtime/bus/actionEvent.mjs
  validates and normalizes action-event envelopes only

runtime/bus/actionEventHistory.mjs
  bounded retained in-memory history/readback only

runtime/bus/actionEventSubscriptionRegistry.mjs
  live same-process listener registry/filtering/publication only

runtime/bus/actionEventReplay.mjs
  optional retained replay/live-join orchestration only

runtime/bus/actionStreamDeltaEvents.mjs
  live-only action.stream.delta mapping from injected parent-side stream observations only

runtime/bus/actionEventLog/actionEventLogStoreContract.mjs
  durable event-log adapter contract, append/read validation, cursor/result shape validation, and high-volume event policy only

runtime/bus/actionEventLog/actionEventLogIntegration.mjs
  optional runtime append handoff to an injected event-log adapter, no-op by default, non-fatal append failure observation only
```

No broad event manager was introduced.

---

## 7. Integration helper implementation details

The integration helper stays modular and owns only the optional append handoff from runtime publication to an injected event-log adapter.

The helper behavior is intentionally narrow:

```text
validates adapter shape through the existing event-log store contract
defaults to no adapter / no-op behavior
skips high-volume events unless explicitly enabled
observes append errors non-fatally
supports synchronous append result observation
supports asynchronous append result observation
does not select a database backend
does not select a file backend
does not implement eventLogStoreBackend
does not own runtime event history, live subscriptions, replay, stream-delta observation, worker lifecycle, or public APIs
```

This branch therefore creates a modular runtime handoff seam, not a storage implementation.

---

## 8. Behavior details

### 8.1 Default runtime behavior

`runtime.mjs` now creates:

```js
const actionEventLog = createActionEventLogIntegration();
```

Because no adapter is provided, `appendRuntimeActionEventLog(...)` skips with reason:

```text
no_adapter
```

This means the branch does not make events durable.

### 8.2 Publication order

`publishRuntimeActionEvent(event)` now preserves the existing record-before-live-publish order:

```text
recordActionEvent(actionEventHistory, event)
appendRuntimeActionEventLog(actionEventLog, recordedEvent)
publishActionEvent(actionEvents, recordedEvent)
```

The durable append handoff receives the recorded/normalized event, including any in-memory sequence assigned by `actionEventHistory`.

### 8.3 Append failure policy

Append errors are non-fatal by default.

The helper can call an optional `onAppendError(err, context)` observer, but observer failures are swallowed so event-log append problems cannot change execute-action behavior.

### 8.4 Async adapter posture

The helper accepts sync or promise-like adapter `appendEvent(entry)` results.

Promise-like results are observed through a returned settlement promise in the helper result, but runtime publication does not await that promise in the default no-adapter composition.

### 8.5 High-volume event posture

`action.stream.delta` remains high-volume excluded by default.

The integration helper skips high-volume events unless explicitly configured with `includeHighVolumeEvents: true`, and that requires an adapter advertising `capabilities.highVolumeEvents: true`.

Runtime stream deltas still use the existing live-only publication path and do not call the event-log integration seam.

