## 14. Caveats / known risks

### Finding: No concrete durable adapter is configured

Affected surface:

```text
eventLogStoreBackend, database/file persistence, restart recovery
```

Why it matters:

```text
The runtime now has an optional append handoff seam, but the default runtime composition still uses no adapter and therefore does not persist events.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Use a separate backend contract/adapter branch to add a real eventLogStoreBackend target after adapter lifecycle, failure policy, and DB target are approved.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Future backend behavior with a real async storage adapter and real-runtime execution.
```

### Finding: Append is non-blocking / non-fatal by design

Affected surface:

```text
audit strictness, guaranteed durability, adapter failure reporting
```

Why it matters:

```text
The current helper intentionally protects execute-action behavior from durable append failures. This is correct for this branch but not sufficient for strict audit requirements.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
If strict durability is required later, define an explicit policy branch with blocking/fail-closed semantics rather than changing this no-op/default seam by accident.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
Whether future use cases need best-effort, buffered, retrying, degraded, or fail-closed append policy.
```

### Finding: docs/dev-notes.60 status needs refresh on branch

Affected surface:

```text
branch documentation only
```

Why it matters:

```text
The original branch doc was written before GitHub upload and before Michael's deterministic/real-runtime checks. It can understate completed gates.
```

Smallest safe correction:

```text
Upload this refreshed dev-notes.60 content or equivalent status refresh to docs/dev-notes.60.
```

What still needs verification:

```text
After upload, inspect docs/dev-notes.60 directly on GitHub to confirm the branch status is current.
```

